Not good advice. First you should note that hard gems and appropriate
rings require ONE turn for EACH character, so those are applicable
only in advance, while writing in the dust the whole E-word requires
ONE turn. Second, writing safely TWO Elbereths seem to require special
conditions[*]; I recall I've read in the code (long ago, though) that
you can only write up to 10 characters in one turn - having speed may
influence that, but here we're talking about normal situations, I'd
presume -, writing more will make it possible for monsters to attack
you, and that, strangely, even if you already have one functional E-Word
written down; I observed[**] exactly that also in the OP's game that I
mentioned upthread. Writing in the dust, say, 16 E-words obviously also
gets ERASED quite quickly after one or two attacks, while a single hard
engraving lasts many MANY turns; that is, of course, only relevant if
you want to fight from such a spot. For just scaring the monsters and
for instant safety in non-foreseeable situation, as initially said, one
would have write in the dust anyway.

